  }, "4. The Search for Enablement: The Partner as an Extrinsic Somatic Safety Loop"), mdx("p", null, "In a healthy relational model, the primary purpose of pair-bonding is mutual, ventral co-regulation. Two sovereign nervous systems come together, drop their defensive armor, and use their presence to soothe each other\u2019s stress, lower heart rates, and provide a somatic sanctuary from the demands of the world. This is ", mdx("strong", {
